1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:02,760
What if a black hole passed through?

2
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:05,000
There's one out there right now.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:13,520
In 2022, astronomers found the first black hole drifting alone through space, about 5,000 light-years away.

4
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:16,840
Our galaxy could hold about 100 million more.

5
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:19,160
Now imagine one heading our way.

6
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:20,680
You wouldn't see it coming.

7
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:25,880
It gives off no light at all. You'd only see the stars bending around it.

8
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:31,160
A black hole 7 times heavier than the Sun is only about 40 km wide.

9
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:33,040
It doesn't even need to hit us.

10
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:35,400
Its gravity rips the Moon away.

11
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:38,120
Then it throws Earth out of its orbit.

12
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:42,680
Morning never comes. The Sun is just a bright star now.

13
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:46,760
Within about a week, the whole planet would be colder than a freezer: below −18°C.

14
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:49,720
The lights go out. The oceans freeze over.

15
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:54,120
Then the air itself starts to freeze. It falls like snow.

16
00:00:54,120 --> 00:01:00,240
Nitrogen, most of the air we breathe, freezes at −210°C.

17
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:02,440
Earth is a rogue planet now.

18
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:05,720
Rogue planets may outnumber the stars in our galaxy.

19
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:09,360
No sunlight. No air. No sound.

20
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:11,250
Nothing could survive out here.

21
00:01:12,620 --> 00:01:14,126
Nothing human.

22
00:01:15,902 --> 00:01:17,922
Wait.

23
00:01:18,422 --> 00:01:21,522
What if Earth stopped spinning?

24
00:01:22,122 --> 00:01:25,750
What if a black hole passed through?
